      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The Colorado Avalanche, a roster hit hard at the worst possible time, saw their playoff hopes crumble. After a mid-season firing, the veteran coach brought in to steady a sinking ship guided them on a strong close. But in the Western Conference Final, the team that finished the job against a depleted opponent took control. Injuries to key personnel had gutted their chances, and a team that got a clear path to the Cup Final thanks to a weakened bracket capitalized, finishing the job in four straight to advance.",
