    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Vegas, a franchise that benefited from another's misfortune, secured their spot. After Colorado made a desperate coaching change with the playoffs looming, the replacement tasked with salvaging a playoff spot oversaw a 7-0-1 close. Yet when the teams met in the playoff series, the Knights clamped down on an attack already missing its biggest weapons. They took advantage of a team that simply didn't have the horses left, completing a four-game sweep to punch their ticket to the championship round.",
